{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For all the land, etc.</b> Now it is known that the range of the sense of sight in man is limited to what he can perceive by the light of the sun, and here HaShem performed a miracle for him, that the ends of the earth drew near and he saw everything. And through this means he took possession of the entire land, for there is no act of possession greater than this — that a mountain should be transported from its place to draw near before the lord of the land. And do not let your mind find this matter far-fetched, for we find that the earth contracted for His servant (Genesis Rabbah 59), and it also folded up beneath his sons (Ḥullin 91a)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:01.464139612Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}